From 68b58b27163ff4fa7fcc5bda16a9732f66d40cc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:00:36 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] [guilib] Settle subpixel textures a moment after they
 stop

Deciding "moving" from one render to the next snaps the texture
whenever a render sees the rect it saw last time: a repeated frame
time, an easing step too small to change the rect, or a second render
of the same frame (stereo 3D draws each eye, dirty-region solvers 1 and
2 draw each region), which then mismatches the first. Decide it once
per frame in Process() instead, keep the fractional position for 200 ms
after the last change, and dirty the texture once when it snaps.

Assisted-By: Claude
---
 xbmc/guilib/GUIImage.dox   |  2 +-
 xbmc/guilib/GUITexture.cpp | 38 +++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 xbmc/guilib/GUITexture.h   |  6 ++++--
 3 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

